     "Add the pinned immutable Probetron node image, so one documented command turns a Debian 13 arm64 host into a Raspberry Pi 4 appliance that builds nothing, stores nothing, and asks the internet for nothing.\n\nRecord every pinned input in image/pins.edn: the rpi-image-gen revision, a Debian Trixie arm64 snapshot and its SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH, and the aarch64 Babashka and probe-rs archives with their SHA-256 digests.\nPin probe-rs 0.32, and state that a later pin belongs there only once hardware qualification records it.\n\nDescribe the appliance to rpi-image-gen in image/config/probetron.yaml and five named layers, each owning one runtime invariant and keeping its static files in a matching .rootfs-overlay tree.\nprobetron-runtime unpacks the release archive under /usr/local, installs the verified Babashka and probe-rs binaries, and installs every other program that the node names by absolute path.\nprobetron-access takes back the general sudo permission and sudo group membership that the base layer grants, leaves bench one passwordless rule for /usr/local/sbin/probetron-node, locks the account while the generated key keeps an unrestricted shell with forwarding, sets a public-key-only sshd policy with keepalives and no DNS, bakes one host identity because a read-only /etc cannot make one, and serves the private half of that key over a socat HTTP service that answers /probetron_key alone as an unprivileged account.\nprobetron-hardware enables SPI0, moves the PL011 onto GPIO14 and GPIO15, removes the serial console, leaves GPIO26 free, and reserves every target device from bench through udev rules that also name /dev/spidev_swd0.\nprobetron-immutable mounts root and boot read-only, masks the remount that /etc/fstab would otherwise win, sizes a tmpfs for /tmp, /var/tmp, /var/log, and /run/probetron, fixes the node identity at build time, and keeps the journal in memory.\nprobetron-offline masks every package, time, discovery, and maintenance unit and turns off the radios, leaving wired DHCP and SSH untouched.\n\nAdd scripts/image.clj as the build driver behind bb image and mise run image.\nGate the platform and the GLIBC that pinned probe-rs needs before any download, fetch or reuse the pinned rpi-image-gen checkout as an ordinary clone under ignored .cache/, and run rpi-image-gen's own layer lint, configuration parse, and layer resolution.\nStop there for --validate-only, which prints the valid-configuration line and exits before keys, staging, privilege, or construction, so ordinary bb test and any checkout avoid the privileged multi-gigabyte build.\nOtherwise verify every fetched archive against its pinned digest before use, generate one SSH keypair per build, run the image generator, and publish build/probetron-rpi4.img.xz and its checksum through a temporary neighbour and one rename each, so an interrupted build replaces neither a valid image nor a valid checksum.\n\nLeave :usb-port-label and :usb-kernels nil, because recording them needs a CDC DUT in the designated Pi 4B receptacle and an udevadm attribute walk that no host here can perform.\nMake both bb image and the hardware layer refuse to proceed while they are unrecorded, and name that measurement as the repair, rather than complete the layer with an inferred topology.\nValidation is unaffected, because the configuration and the layers are complete and the measurement is the only thing missing.",
