     "Add a deterministic release task that packages Probetron into a tagged-release archive.\n\nIntroduce `probetron.archive`, a pure encoder that turns archive members into USTAR, gzip, and SHA-256 bytes with a fixed mode, owner, and modification time, so the same members always encode to the same bytes and no clock or machine identity reaches a release.\n\nIntroduce `probetron.package`, which holds the pure release plan and the imperative shell that writes it.\nThe shell reads the VERSION file and the source tree and hands their contents to `plan`, which reads nothing itself.\nThe plan requires `probetron.version` to repeat the declared version and accepts an explicit release tag only when that tag names the same version with or without its leading `v`.\nIt lays out `bin/probetron`, `bin/probetron-node`, the relocatable `lib/probetron/` source tree, `VERSION`, and `README.md` in one sorted order, gives the two entry points mode 0755 and everything else mode 0644, and refuses any member path that is absolute, that leaves the archive root, or that a tar name field cannot hold.\nThe shell then writes `build/probetron-<version>.tar.gz` and a `sha256sum`-readable checksum file, refuses an archive that would land outside the build directory, and names the missing file and the corrective action when a source or the VERSION file cannot be read.\nThe archive carries no platform Babashka binary and no test tree, so one archive serves macOS and Linux alike.\n\nDeclare `--tag` as a value option, as every other Probetron command line declares one, so a `--tag` without a value gives back a usage error instead of a stack trace.\n\nKeep `scripts/package.clj` as a thin entry point that does nothing but hand the command line to `probetron.package`, expose it as `bb package` and `mise run package`, and lint the new script directory alongside `src` and `test`.\n\nCover the release through the public `probetron.package` namespace: package twice into a temporary build directory and compare digests, check the archive listing and the checksum file, extract the archive and run both entry points' `--help` through the pinned Babashka runtime, and check that a mismatched tag, a valueless `--tag`, and an escaping archive name all fail.\n\nDocument the build task, the determinism rules, and the archive layout that a future mise GitHub tool installs on `PATH`.",
