     "Add the short target operations to the node so info, flash, erase, and reset drive the RP2350 through the direct Linux SPI probe.\n\nInline the one DUT slot in a pure probetron.node.hardware namespace, which holds every device, executable, selector, service port, upload path, and limit, and builds the probe-rs and gpioset argv vectors with the explicit probe selector, the SWD protocol, and the caller-supplied chip and speed.\nCarry those constants into the node runtime, so production always takes the fixed absolute paths while a test substitutes a temporary appliance.\n\nValidate one uploaded firmware image in a pure probetron.node.elf namespace.\nIt requires the complete ELF32 little-endian header, the header, program-entry, and section-entry sizes of the ELF specification, and an ARM or RISC-V machine, and it refuses a program or section table and a load segment that reads outside the upload.\nEvery declared offset is a long, so no size can overflow into a range that looks like it fits.\n\nAssemble the information record in a pure probetron.node.information namespace, which renders the same facts as concise text or as EDN with stable keyword keys.\n\nCarry the operations out in probetron.node.target.\ninfo holds the transaction lock while it reports Probetron, Babashka, probe-rs, the operating system, and the node identity, and asks probe-rs what sits on the SWD bus.\nflash reads standard input into a unique file under the bounded volatile upload directory, stops one byte past the limit, refuses an oversized or malformed upload before probe-rs opens the target, and removes the file on every exit path, including a handled shutdown.\nOnly a verified download pulses the RUN line, so a failed flash leaves the target where it was.\nerase delegates once to probe-rs and gives back its status without a second destructive attempt, and reset holds GPIO26 low for a 100 ms gpioset pulse instead of asking probe-rs.\nA missing SPI device, GPIO chip, probe-rs, or gpioset stops the operation before any process starts, and the diagnostic names the resource and the repair.\n\nRaise the public ELF bound to the documented 64 MiB, so the client and the node refuse the same uploads for the same reason.\n\nCover all of it with tests that drive the public node runner over a temporary appliance and fake absolute-command adapters, proving exact argv, information formats, subprocess status propagation, upload cleanup, flash-reset ordering, and rejection of truncated tables, out-of-range load segments, and oversized uploads before any process launches.",
